## Advantages

- Non-invasive screening approach
- Uses readily available patient information
- Improves clinical decision support
- Reduces unnecessary diagnostic procedures

---

## Limitations

- Single-center dataset
- Moderate sensitivity
- Dataset not publicly available
- Requires external validation on larger populations

---

## Conclusion

The study demonstrated that machine learning models, especially XGBoost, can accurately predict probable Chronic Rhinosinusitis using patient-generated health data before specialist evaluation. This approach may help clinicians prioritize referrals, optimize imaging utilization, and improve early diagnosis of CRS.

